{
  "$comment": "A-16: THE Devices page row, one spec ×4 (web my-machines.tsx, desktop machines.rs, iOS AgentsView, Android AgentsScreen). One LINE per device: kind glyph, name, version (warning tone when the caller's own device is outdated), the default star, the Shared / This device tags, the status line (Online / Last seen …) under the name; then ONE chip per login (brand mark + label + ` · plan` when the label is an email), in `sortDeviceLogins` order; then the attention icon, only when `attention` is non-empty; then the settings gear (own registered rows; hover-revealed on a pointer, always on touch). Nothing folds and no warning is written inline. A login chip previews its limits: the account picker's hover card (UsageWindows `hover` density) on a pointer; on touch, and on a pointer click, the chip opens the account menu (Sign in / Sign out / Remove account, the existing AccountChipMenu rules) with those same bars at its top. A team device's chips preview but never open a menu. Own, online rows with an agent to add end the chip row with a ghost `+` (Add account). A device that reported accounts but holds NO login says `noAccount` muted in the chip slot; a device that never reported says `checking`. The attention icon (warning tone) opens a small card on hover (pointer) or tap (touch): one line per item, `text` left, its one `action` pill right (null = no pill). Items in order: every login whose health is needs_relogin, then every signed_out login, then the update line. An AGENT with no login at all (a CLI installed, never signed in: `profiles` empty or absent) is NOT an item and badges nothing: that is the old IDE bug where mint read `Signed out` because Codex was installed. The update line exists only on the caller's own device: `updateQueued` when an update is parked behind live sessions (no action), else `updateAvailable` (with `latest`) when the client's own version compare says `outdated` (action `update` only for a SERVER — the CLI daemon is the one device that acts on an update request; a desktop app updates itself, so its line carries no action — and only while it is online and registered). Login actions (`sign_in`) only on the caller's own online device. Groups: online rows first in the list's own order, then under the muted `offline` label every offline row, dimmed. The same rules hold for the Team devices section (read-only: no gear, no `+`, no actions, a team owner's Remove keeps the gear's slot).",
